package patterncatalyst:cargo-kafka-handler@0.1.0;

/// The ch23 Kafka message HANDLER for the cargo domain, as a WebAssembly
/// component — the workload KEDA's `kafka` ScaledObject observes and the wadm
/// spreadscaler OWNS the replica count for (see ../k8s/wasmcloud/wadm-kafka.yaml
/// and ../k8s/keda/base/kafka-scaledobject.yaml).
///
/// This world EXPORTS `wasmcloud:messaging/handler@0.2.0` — the interface the
/// wasmCloud `messaging-kafka` capability provider invokes once per delivered
/// Kafka message (the provider is the CONSUMER that owns the subscription;
/// this component is the business-logic HANDLER wadm links it to, the same
/// provider-calls-component shape as the httpserver/cargo-http link in Part 4).
/// It also exports `wasmcloud:messaging/types` (the `broker-message` record
/// handler.wit's `use` pulls in) — exported explicitly alongside handler,
/// matching the house convention of always listing a types-only interface a
/// world's functional interfaces depend on (see contracts/wit/world.wit:
/// `export types; export booking; export handling;`).
///
/// It IMPORTS the cargo domain's `handling` interface (+ the pure-type
/// `types`) from the repository contract and calls `register-handling-event`
/// on every delivered message — a real write against the SAME cargo domain
/// Parts 2-5 use, not a stub. In the wasmCloud lattice this import is
/// satisfied at wadm deploy time by a `link` trait to a deployed cargo
/// provider component (the runtime-link shape from ch20's
/// wadm-filtered.yaml), NOT by a `wac plug` composition — this component is
/// deployed standalone, never composed into one .wasm with the provider.
///
/// `wasmcloud:messaging@0.2.0` is vendored under wit/deps/messaging (the
/// upstream wasmCloud/messaging WIT package, verbatim). `patterncatalyst:cargo`
/// is a path dependency to the repository contract (Cargo.toml) — the contract
/// stays byte-for-byte pristine; this component defines only its own world.
world cargo-kafka-handler {
    export wasmcloud:messaging/types@0.2.0;
    export wasmcloud:messaging/handler@0.2.0;

    import patterncatalyst:cargo/types@0.1.0;
    import patterncatalyst:cargo/handling@0.1.0;
}
